{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And one who eats from its carcass, and one who carries its carcass.</b> One law applies to both of them: this one carries outdoors and that one carries indoors. One should not say: let Scripture be silent about his washing his garments in the first instance and say thus: 'and one who eats its carcass and one who carries its carcass shall wash his garments and be impure until evening' — since the one who eats comes to give the measure for one who touches and one who carries, as Rashi explained, Scripture needed to spell out each law separately."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:32.844728568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}